- (new) The chart lists July -10,000 and August +133,000. The text only gives August's first figure, 162,000, and says "60,000 lower". The revised monthly figures are never stated, so I could not reconcile them.
- (repeat, r0) "so most of the visible tenth is rounding". The unrounded 4.141% to 4.175% is a move of 0.034 points. I had to work out what that does to the 0.1 headline change.
- (repeat, r0) Three averages: "That 45,000 is the prior 12 months; the Associated Press put average gains at 68,000 jobs a month so far this year, and 2025 at 9,700 jobs a month." Nothing says how they relate.
- (repeat, r0) "The newest count is August's, when hires changed little at 5.2 million." It sits unexplained among calendar dates.
